{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774114537,"nonce":"nBU7Qcv2s+M5mNKZUuDDcGkKAKY=","title":"Automated CLAUDE.md restructure via SDK agent in Presets tab","message":"When a user imports a CLAUDE.md (or any Markdown convention file) into the Presets tab, Mandible should offer to automatically restructure it so every leaf node is self-contained (self-descriptive headings, scope sentences, explicit dependencies).\n\n**Flow:**\n1. User imports a CLAUDE.md file into the Presets tab\n2. A spinner/placeholder appears in the sidebar for that preset\n3. In the background, Mandible spawns an SDK agent session that restructures the file using the same principles as the manual Track A restructure (c6590fe)\n4. While the agent works, the user can click a button on the sidebar item to navigate to the agent chat session and watch it work\n5. When the agent finishes, the spinner becomes a real preset item in the sidebar\n6. The user can then browse the restructured preset in the tree editor\n\n**Backend:**\n- New endpoint to trigger restructuring (spawns an SDK session with a specific prompt)\n- The prompt encodes the restructuring principles: self-contained leaves, self-descriptive headings, explicit dependency references, scope sentences\n- Session should be visible in the Chat tab (it is a real SDK session, just auto-spawned)\n\n**Frontend (Presets sidebar):**\n- Two states for the sidebar item: \"restructuring...\" (spinner + link to agent session) and \"ready\" (normal preset item)\n- Clicking the spinner state navigates to the agent session in the Chat tab\n- Session stays in background unless user clicks — no auto-navigation\n\n**Design decisions:**\n- Agent session is a first-class SDK session, visible in Chat tab\n- The restructuring prompt should be a built-in preset/template in Mandible, not hardcoded in the endpoint\n- This generalizes beyond CLAUDE.md — any imported convention file can be restructured\n\n**Relationship to Track A (c6590fe):**\nTrack A is the manual first-pass restructure of the actual CLAUDE.md in dotfiles. This issue is the automated, reusable version built into Mandible. Track A produces the restructuring principles; this issue productionizes them as an agent workflow.\n\nThis is Mandible code (backend + frontend), not dotfiles. Should be a new partition (Track D) under the phase 2 umbrella (e866450), or standalone work after current tracks complete.","files":null}]}